        "content": "<p>I'm getting a modpost error when build testing for arm32:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>ERROR: modpost: drivers/pwm/pwm_th1520.ko: symbol '__aeabi_uldivmod' undefined!\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Looks like a 64 bit division on 32 bit hardware, probably this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">ns_to_cycles</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ns</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rate_hz</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NSEC_PER_SEC_U64</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">NSEC_PER_SEC</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ns</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">saturating_mul</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">rate_hz</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NSEC_PER_SEC_U64</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">cycles_to_ns</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cycles</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u32</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rate_hz</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NSEC_PER_SEC_U64</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">NSEC_PER_SEC</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">u64</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">from</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cycles</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NSEC_PER_SEC_U64</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"n\">div_ceil</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">rate_hz</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I'm not usually building for arm32, so I'm wondering if it is user error on my end.  But I seem to recall that 64 bit division on 32 bit hardware is a no-go, is that correct? Should the driver be gated on <code>CONFIG_64BIT</code>?</p>",
